# Environment
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audio, and anything derived closely enough from it to count as a copy.
#
# The project's rule: do not redistribute audio; ship extracted features plus a
# script that regenerates them from source URLs. The
# note-level transcriptions are excluded under the same rule rather than merely
# for size -- a per-note dump of onsets, pitches and velocities is a close
# derivative of the recording, and some of the archival sources are
# in-copyright commercial releases with no license statement. The aggregate
# feature vectors in results/*_features.npz are what gets shipped instead, and
# they are enough to reproduce every number in the README.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/audio/
data/audio/candidates/
results/tier2_modern_notes/
results/tier3_notes/
results/note_cache/
results/transcriptions/

# Third-party datasets, fetched by script rather than vendored.
# ASAP performance MIDI: scripts/verification.py and the tier pipelines fetch
# what they need on demand.
data/asap/

# Bulk third-party metadata, regenerated by scripts/resolve_candidates.py and
# scripts/survey_pianists.py.
results/archive_meta/

# Caches: large, machine-specific, and rebuilt on demand.
results/dtw_cache/
results/dtw_cache_op23/
results/fingerprints/
results/dedup/

# Session exports: the 3 MB machine format behind the working notes.
docs/*.zip

# Transient run artifacts: completion markers, stderr files, and the logs of
# interrupted runs. One of these mattered rather than merely being untidy --
# the interrupted pooled-scaling log carries numbers that are not reported as
# results anywhere, because the permutation null that would
# validate them never ran. Committing it would put unvalidated figures in the
# repository where a reader could mistake them for findings.
*.done
*.err
results/tier2_strict_*.log
results/tier2_wide_pipeline.log

# Session transcripts. Internal working records, not project documentation.
docs/session-*

# Working notes. The write-ups, the plan and the Q&A are kept locally for
# reference but are not part of the published repo, which is the README, the
# code and the feature vectors needed to reproduce it.
/DATA.md
/PROJECT_PLAN.md
data/SOURCES.md
docs/QA.md
results/*.md
